WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.212 --> 00:00:01.419
- I hate being cold.

00:00:01.419 --> 00:00:02.505
Like I'm from the desert

00:00:02.505 --> 00:00:05.156
and cold is just not
something that I'm into.

00:00:05.156 --> 00:00:08.994
- I actually have kind of
like a achy, bruised knee,

00:00:08.994 --> 00:00:11.993
and I'm really hoping that
it's gonna magically fix it.

00:00:11.993 --> 00:00:13.341
- My biggest fear would be like my fingers

00:00:13.341 --> 00:00:16.383
getting really cold, and like falling off.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.647
- I went skydiving before.

00:00:17.647 --> 00:00:18.829
I think I can do this.

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:23.619
(techno music)

00:00:42.622 --> 00:00:44.620
- So basically, what you
guys are gonna be doing today

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.107
is you're going to be gonna
be going into a chamber.

00:00:46.107 --> 00:00:48.684
It's negative 220 degrees.

00:00:48.684 --> 00:00:50.842
Some risks associated with this

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:54.220
could be frostbite, skin
burns and irritations,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.380
but, we don't let you
go in for long enough

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:57.679
for that even to happen,

00:00:57.679 --> 00:00:59.641
so we're gonna put you in
for a safe amount of time.

00:00:59.641 --> 00:01:00.918
It's a minute-and-a-half.

00:01:00.918 --> 00:01:03.159
A minute-and-a-half sounds
like a very short time,

00:01:03.159 --> 00:01:05.445
but it'll be the longest
minute-and-a-half of your life.

00:01:05.445 --> 00:01:08.429
- I honestly feel like I'm
in line for a roller coaster.

00:01:10.646 --> 00:01:11.725
- Ready.

00:01:11.725 --> 00:01:13.546
- Oh, she's ready.

00:01:13.546 --> 00:01:15.631
- Well, I'm getting naked for a video.

00:01:17.873 --> 00:01:19.405
- Just another day at work.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.954
What if I pee my pants while I'm in there?

00:01:25.954 --> 00:01:28.129
- I was literally just thinking that!

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:32.969
(dramatic music)

00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:42.251
(screams)
- [Voiceover] 10 seconds.

00:01:44.214 --> 00:01:46.246
- You know what? This
is no big deal, guys.

00:01:46.246 --> 00:01:47.089
Oh, is it getting colder?

00:01:47.089 --> 00:01:48.052
- [Voiceover] I'm gonna turn it on now.

00:01:48.052 --> 00:01:50.106
- Oh, he's turning it on now.
- [Voiceover] I'm joking.

00:01:50.798 --> 00:01:51.461
- Is it cold yet?

00:01:51.461 --> 00:01:52.803
- Oh, my goodness, it's so cold.

00:01:52.803 --> 00:01:54.963
- I don't think I've ever
been this cold in my life.

00:01:54.963 --> 00:01:56.474
- [Voiceover] Oh, my gosh.

00:01:57.621 --> 00:01:59.132
- It's so cold.

00:01:59.723 --> 00:02:01.397
Okay, oh my god.

00:02:06.562 --> 00:02:07.966
- Very cool.

00:02:07.966 --> 00:02:10.233
So now we're going into the Cryo M3,

00:02:10.233 --> 00:02:12.149
which is the meat locker version

00:02:12.149 --> 00:02:13.849
of the cryochamber.

00:02:20.278 --> 00:02:22.715
- The cold happens in here, actually.

00:02:22.715 --> 00:02:23.707
When you open this door, you get welcomed

00:02:23.707 --> 00:02:25.995
by this big cloud of cold air.

00:02:25.995 --> 00:02:27.631
Again, minus 220 below.

00:02:27.631 --> 00:02:28.824
So, who's first?

00:02:29.589 --> 00:02:34.501
(dramatic music)

00:02:35.854 --> 00:02:37.827
(scream)

00:02:42.547 --> 00:02:43.691
- That's a human test.

00:02:43.691 --> 00:02:45.108
- There was something nice and comforting

00:02:45.108 --> 00:02:46.481
about being in there.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.537
- Oh, yes.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.020
Oh, yeah.

00:02:53.982 --> 00:02:58.244
Oh, I can kinda feel the
mucus in my nose crisp up.

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:01.261
Hello, Clarice.

00:03:01.261 --> 00:03:03.197
That was cool. I liked that a lot.

00:03:06.172 --> 00:03:07.352
(scream)

00:03:07.352 --> 00:03:09.020
(laughing)

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:12.407
- [Voiceover] Three, two, one.

00:03:12.407 --> 00:03:14.520
Time is up. Please exit the chamber.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.517
- I can't speak, my brain's frozen.

00:03:16.517 --> 00:03:17.841
There she goes.

00:03:17.841 --> 00:03:18.896
- [Voiceover] Oh, my god!

00:03:18.896 --> 00:03:21.268
Oh, my god!

00:03:22.578 --> 00:03:24.238
Oh my god, oh my god, oh my god.

00:03:24.238 --> 00:03:25.817
It's so cold.

00:03:25.817 --> 00:03:27.946
- I think we all know who the wuss is.

00:03:27.946 --> 00:03:30.110
- It's so cold.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.188
- [Voiceover] This one
or the other one worse?

00:03:33.975 --> 00:03:35.347
- I think this one.

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:37.106
- Usually I can't touch my toes.

00:03:37.927 --> 00:03:40.671
Bingo, that's cryo.

00:03:41.585 --> 00:03:44.515
Being outside in Boston
in the winter for an hour

00:03:44.515 --> 00:03:47.356
was worse than being in there
for a minute-and-a-half.

00:03:47.356 --> 00:03:48.701
- It was by far the coldest

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.315
that I've ever been in my entire life.

00:03:50.315 --> 00:03:52.138
- It was definitely
invigorating and refreshing.

00:03:52.138 --> 00:03:54.762
- I would do it again, I mean if

00:03:54.762 --> 00:03:57.173
I see a change or feel
a really big difference

00:03:57.173 --> 00:03:59.552
I would definitely want to come back.

00:03:59.552 --> 00:04:01.770
So, maybe this weekend.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:06.564
(techno music)

